From: Helder Correia <heldercorreia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: list fallbacks without populating fonts when any will do

fallbacksForFamily() called the default implementation, which populates
every family, and populating opens every font file. One requested family
that isn't installed, or one glyph the font lacks, therefore opened all
fonts on the GUI thread. It took 0.62 s for 359 font files and 0.35 s for
528, in warm starts on two Windows machines.

When the script has no writing system to filter by, every family is a
candidate, so the list needs only the family names. These are known without
populating, and QFontEngineMulti loads each fallback only when the ones
before it lack a glyph. Scripts with a writing system still use the default
implementation, which needs the writing system of each family.

Together with the previous patch, a warm start with 1766 families went from
3.03 s to 0.35 s and opened 16 font files instead of 1149, also when the
requested family wasn't installed.
---
--- a/src/gui/text/windows/qwindowsdirectwritefontdatabase.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/text/windows/qwindowsdirectwritefontdatabase.cpp
@@ -389,7 +389,30 @@ QStringList QWindowsDirectWriteFontDatabase::fallbacksForFamily(const QString &f
     result.append(QWindowsFontDatabaseBase::familiesForScript(script));
     result.append(familyForStyleHint(styleHint));
     result.append(extraTryFontsForFamily(family));
-    result.append(QPlatformFontDatabase::fallbacksForFamily(family, style, styleHint, script));
+
+    const auto writingSystem = qt_writing_system_for_script(script);
+    if (writingSystem == QFontDatabase::Any
+        || writingSystem >= QFontDatabase::WritingSystemsCount) {
+        // Every family is a candidate here, so no family needs populating.
+        // QFontEngineMulti loads a fallback only when the ones before it lack
+        // a glyph, while populating every family opens every font file, which
+        // takes most of a second even when the first fallback has the glyph.
+        // Bitmap fonts go last, as in the default implementation.
+        auto *db = QFontDatabasePrivate::instance();
+        QStringList bitmapFamilies;
+        for (int i = 0; i < db->count; ++i) {
+            const QtFontFamily *f = db->families[i];
+            if (f->populated && f->count == 0)
+                continue;
+            if (m_populatedBitmapFonts.contains(f->name))
+                bitmapFamilies.append(f->name);
+            else
+                result.append(f->name);
+        }
+        result.append(bitmapFamilies);
+    } else {
+        result.append(QPlatformFontDatabase::fallbacksForFamily(family, style, styleHint, script));
+    }
 
     qCDebug(lcQpaFonts) << __FUNCTION__ << family << style << styleHint
         << script << result;
